# Functional Specification: Context-Aware Task Execution with Smart Subagent Spawning

## Context

**Problem:** Large plans exhaust context before completion, requiring manual /clear calls between implementation waves. Task 029 (13 tasks, 630 lines) required several waves due to context exhaustion. Even with Claude Code's auto-compaction, task-specific details (line numbers, code snippets in action blocks) get lost during summarization.

**Value:**
- Seamless execution of large plans without user intervention
- Each task gets fresh subagent context with exactly what it needs
- Main conversation stays lean for orchestration (~15% context)
- No reliance on auto-compaction as a feature
- Foundation for future parallel task execution

## Scope

### In Scope
- Modify festina-implement to spawn subagents for task execution
- Modify festina-plan to generate explicit `<context>` blocks per task
- Add CLI commands for extracting individual task context from plans
- Update plan.xml template schema with `<context>` element

### Out of Scope
- Parallel task execution (sequential only in this iteration)
- Dynamic context estimation/token counting
- Changes to task.xml or spec.xml formats
- Complexity-based routing (simple inline vs complex subagent) — all tasks use subagents

## Functional Requirements

- FR1: festina-implement SHALL spawn a separate subagent (general-purpose type) for each plan task
- FR2: Each subagent SHALL receive explicit file references to read, not embedded code snippets
- FR3: Each subagent SHALL execute the task action, run verification, and report success/failure
- FR4: The orchestrator SHALL persist task completion to plan.xml after each subagent finishes
- FR5: The orchestrator SHALL stay under 30% context usage throughout execution
- FR6: festina-plan SHALL generate `<context>` blocks for each task containing files to read
- FR7: The `<context>` block SHALL include: existing files to read, pattern reference files, dependent file imports
- FR8: CLI SHALL provide commands to extract individual task context from plan.xml
- FR9: If subagent fails verification after fix attempts, orchestrator SHALL ask user how to proceed
- FR10: Quality verification (TODO scan, requirement trace, wiring check) SHALL run in orchestrator after all tasks complete
- FR11: Directive loading and compliance checking SHALL remain in the orchestrator (not delegated to subagents)

