## Research Findings

### Product Context
- **docs/context-selection**: Tiered loading (minimal/standard/full) ~50-200-1000 tokens per tier
- **tasks/implement**: Current execution is sequential, marks completion per task, code uncommitted

### Engineering Patterns
- **patterns/orchestrator**: Decompose large orchestrators, composition root wires components
- **patterns/subagent-orchestration**: Stub doc to be completed after implementation

### Codebase Analysis
- festina-scope already uses Task tool with parallel subagents
- festina-implement currently executes all tasks in main context
- Plan.xml tasks have self-contained info but no explicit "read these files first" block

### Pitfalls Identified
- **Task complexity threshold**: Decision: Always spawn subagent (every task gets fresh context)
- **Subagent prompt construction**: Decision: Explicit file refs only (subagent reads fresh, lean prompts)
- **Subagents cannot spawn subagents**: Standard mitigation — subagent must complete all work without delegation
- **Context estimation is approximate**: Standard mitigation — orchestrator uses conservative buffer

## Subagent Prompt Template

The orchestrator constructs a prompt for each subagent following this structure:

```
Execute task {id}: "{name}"

**Read these files first:**
{For each file in <context>:}
- {file path}

**Pattern to follow:**
{pattern file path from <pattern> element, if present}

**Action:**
{content of <action> element}

**Verify:** {content of <verify> element}

**Done criteria:** {content of <done> element}

**Spec reference:** .festinalente/tasks/{taskId}/spec.xml
(Read if you need functional requirements or additional context)

When complete, report:
- SUCCESS: {summary of what was done}
- FAILURE: {what failed and why}
```

## Technical Constraints

- Task tool subagent_type must be "general-purpose" for Edit/Write/Bash access
- Subagents cannot spawn subagents (Claude Code limitation)
- Sequential execution respects task dependencies (depends attribute)
- Plan.xml must remain valid XML after context block addition
- Directive loading and compliance checking stays in orchestrator (not passed to subagents)

## Dependencies

### External
- None (uses existing Claude Code Task tool)

### Internal
- festina-plan changes must precede festina-implement changes (plan format must support context blocks)
- CLI changes can be done in parallel with skill changes

## Risks & Mitigations

| Risk | Impact | Mitigation |
|------|--------|------------|
| Subagent fails to complete task | Blocks implementation | Ask user for resolution options (fix manually, skip, stop) |
| Context blocks too large | Defeats purpose of lean orchestrator | File refs only, no embedded content |
| Subagent doesn't follow action instructions | Wrong implementation | Include spec file ref in context for subagent to read |
| Plan.xml parsing breaks with new schema | CLI commands fail | Add context element to existing task schema additively |

